    card title "Do we need bees to eat?"

Do we need bees to eat? Four things people say about bees and our food: true, or myth?
    draw claims_dot_1 claims_dot_2 claims_dot_3 claims_dot_4 parallel true

First: honeybee hives are vanishing around the world.
    draw claims_1

    quiz "Tap True or Myth." on_canvas true buttons_at.x 840 buttons_at.y 420 buttons_layout column reveal.text "MYTH: +85 %" reveal.at.x 190 reveal.at.y 440 reveal.size 48
        right: Myth. Beekeepers kept about eighty-five percent more hives in 2017 than in 1961, thanks above all to Asia.
        * True
        + Myth

Next: without bees, there would be no wheat, rice or maize.
    draw claims_2

    quiz "Tap True or Myth." on_canvas true buttons_at.x 840 buttons_at.y 420 buttons_layout column reveal.text "MYTH: wind" reveal.at.x 190 reveal.at.y 440 reveal.size 48
        right: Myth. Wheat, rice and maize are pollinated by the wind or by themselves; they never needed an insect.
        * True
        + Myth

Third: three in four of the leading food crops need pollinators.
    draw claims_3

    quiz "Tap True or Myth." on_canvas true buttons_at.x 840 buttons_at.y 420 buttons_layout column reveal.text "TRUE: 75 %" reveal.at.x 190 reveal.at.y 440 reveal.size 48
        right: True. About three in four of the leading food crops depend on pollinators, at least in part: apples, almonds, coffee, melons.
        + True
        * Myth

And last: without pollinators, chocolate would be in trouble.
    draw claims_4

    quiz "Tap True or Myth." on_canvas true buttons_at.x 840 buttons_at.y 420 buttons_layout column reveal.text "TRUE: midges!" reveal.at.x 215 reveal.at.y 440 reveal.size 48
        right: True. Cocoa cannot fruit without them, and its pollinators are not bees at all, but tiny flies called midges.
        + True
        * Myth

So pollinators matter, though not for the staples. Now the catch: think of all the food we grow, by weight.
    draw claims_strip plate

Only about a third of it comes from crops that need pollinators at all: fruit, nuts, coffee, cocoa.
    draw third i_apple i_coffee i_choc i_nut t_third t_third2

Lose every pollinator, and studies estimate food production would fall by about five to eight percent.
    draw sliver t_sliver

No famine, then, but a poorer plate, and poorer farmers where those crops are grown.
    highlight sliver t_sliver

